{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01HgQJm2CdntLNn4E5LGPJKx","type":"tool_result","content":"1\tid: srd080-base64\n2\ttitle: \"cmd/base64: Base64 Encode and Decode\"\n3\t\n4\tproblem: |\n5\t  macOS does not ship base64. Scripts that encode or decode Base64 data using the GNU\n6\t  base64 format must use the Homebrew reference binary. The Go implementation must match\n7\t  the Homebrew GNU reference binary (gbase64, installed by coreutils) byte-for-byte on\n8\t  all flag combinations, using encoding/base64 from the Go standard library, verified\n9\t  by differential testing via pkg/testutils.\n10\t\n11\tgoals:\n12\t  - G1: Encode stdin or file contents to Base64 and write to stdout.\n13\t  - G2: Decode Base64-encoded input back to binary with --decode (-d).\n14\t  - G3: Support line wrapping control with --wrap (-w).\n15\t  - G4: Verify functional parity against gbase64 via differential testing.\n16\t\n17\trequirements:\n18\t  R1:\n19\t    title: Encoding\n20\t    items:\n21\t      - R1.1:\n22\t          text: Must read from FILE or stdin (when no file or \"-\" is given) and encode the input using RFC 4648 Base64, writing the result to stdout.\n23\t      - R1.2:\n24\t          text: Must wrap encoded output at 76 characters per line by default.\n25\t      - R1.3:\n26\t          text: \"-w COLS or --wrap=COLS must set the wrap column. -w 0 disables wrapping (single line output).\"\n27\t      - R1.4:\n28\t          text: Must exit 1 when a named file cannot be opened, printing an error to stderr.\n29\t\n30\t  R2:\n31\t    title: Decoding\n32\t    items:\n33\t      - R2.1:\n34\t          text: \"-d or --decode must decode Base64 input from FILE or stdin and write the binary result to stdout.\"\n35\t      - R2.2:\n36\t          text: Must ignore whitespace (newlines, spaces) in the input during decoding.\n37\t      - R2.3:\n38\t          text: \"-i or --ignore-garbage must ignore non-alphabet characters in the input during decoding.\"\n39\t      - R2.4:\n40\t          text: Must exit 1 with an error to stderr when the input contains invalid Base64 characters (without --ignore-garbage).\n41\t\n42\t  R3:\n43\t    title: Exit codes and SIGPIPE\n44\t    items:\n45\t      - R3.1:\n46\t          text: Must exit 0 on successful encoding or decoding.\n47\t      - R3.2:\n48\t          text: Must exit 1 on any error (invalid input, missing file, invalid option).\n49\t      - R3.3:\n50\t          text: Must handle SIGPIPE gracefully (exit 0) using pkg/sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler.\n51\t\n52\tnon_goals:\n53\t  - cmd/base64 does not implement Base64url (URL-safe alphabet).\n54\t  - cmd/base64 does not implement Base32; use base32 for that.\n55\t\n56\tpackage_contract:\n57\t  imports:\n58\t    - github.com/petar-djukic/go-unix-utils/pkg/encutil\n59\t    - github.com/petar-djukic/go-unix-utils/pkg/sys\n60\t\n61\tacceptance_criteria:\n62\t  - id: AC1\n63\t    criterion: \"echo hello | base64 produces Base64 encoded output matching gbase64.\"\n64\t    traces:\n65\t      - R1.1\n66\t      - R1.2\n67\t  - id: AC2\n68\t    criterion: \"echo aGVsbG8= | base64 -d produces 'hello', matching gbase64 -d.\"\n69\t    traces:\n70\t      - R2.1\n71\t      - R2.2\n72\t  - id: AC3\n73\t    criterion: \"Differential test against gbase64 passes for all required test cases.\"\n74\t    traces:\n75\t      - R1.1\n76\t      - R1.2\n77\t      - R1.3\n78\t      - R1.4\n79\t      - R2.1\n80\t      - R2.2\n81\t      - R2.3\n82\t      - R2.4\n83\t  - id: AC4\n84\t    criterion: \"cmd/base64 compiles with no warnings under golangci-lint.\"\n85\t    traces:\n86\t      - R1.1\n87\t      - R1.2\n88\t      - R1.3\n89\t      - R1.4\n90\t      - R2.1\n91\t      - R2.2\n92\t      - R2.3\n93\t      - R2.4\n94\t      - R3.1\n95\t      - R3.2\n96\t      - R3.3\n97\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"94d059ca-d891-4e73-9708-e7fb55a5e120","uuid":"27403ea2-9920-485a-8c07-deb2524b79cd","timestamp":"2026-05-23T11:51:17.735Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/5520/docs/specs/software-requirements/srd080-base64.yaml","content":"id: srd080-base64\ntitle: \"cmd/base64: Base64 Encode and Decode\"\n\nproblem: |\n  macOS does not ship base64. Scripts that encode or decode Base64 data using the GNU\n  base64 format must use the Homebrew reference binary. The Go implementation must match\n  the Homebrew GNU reference binary (gbase64, installed by coreutils) byte-for-byte on\n  all flag combinations, using encoding/base64 from the Go standard library, verified\n  by differential testing via pkg/testutils.\n\ngoals:\n  - G1: Encode stdin or file contents to Base64 and write to stdout.\n  - G2: Decode Base64-encoded input back to binary with --decode (-d).\n  - G3: Support line wrapping control with --wrap (-w).\n  - G4: Verify functional parity against gbase64 via differential testing.\n\nrequirements:\n  R1:\n    title: Encoding\n    items:\n      - R1.1:\n          text: Must read from FILE or stdin (when no file or \"-\" is given) and encode the input using RFC 4648 Base64, writing the result to stdout.\n      - R1.2:\n          text: Must wrap encoded output at 76 characters per line by default.\n      - R1.3:\n          text: \"-w COLS or --wrap=COLS must set the wrap column. -w 0 disables wrapping (single line output).\"\n      - R1.4:\n          text: Must exit 1 when a named file cannot be opened, printing an error to stderr.\n\n  R2:\n    title: Decoding\n    items:\n      - R2.1:\n          text: \"-d or --decode must decode Base64 input from FILE or stdin and write the binary result to stdout.\"\n      - R2.2:\n          text: Must ignore whitespace (newlines, spaces) in the input during decoding.\n      - R2.3:\n          text: \"-i or --ignore-garbage must ignore non-alphabet characters in the input during decoding.\"\n      - R2.4:\n          text: Must exit 1 with an error to stderr when the input contains invalid Base64 characters (without --ignore-garbage).\n\n  R3:\n    title: Exit codes and SIGPIPE\n    items:\n      - R3.1:\n          text: Must exit 0 on successful encoding or decoding.\n      - R3.2:\n          text: Must exit 1 on any error (invalid input, missing file, invalid option).\n      - R3.3:\n          text: Must handle SIGPIPE gracefully (exit 0) using pkg/sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler.\n\nnon_goals:\n  - cmd/base64 does not implement Base64url (URL-safe alphabet).\n  - cmd/base64 does not implement Base32; use base32 for that.\n\npackage_contract:\n  imports:\n    - github.com/petar-djukic/go-unix-utils/pkg/encutil\n    - github.com/petar-djukic/go-unix-utils/pkg/sys\n\nacceptance_criteria:\n  - id: AC1\n    criterion: \"echo hello | base64 produces Base64 encoded output matching gbase64.\"\n    traces:\n      - R1.1\n      - R1.2\n  - id: AC2\n    criterion: \"echo aGVsbG8= | base64 -d produces 'hello', matching gbase64 -d.\"\n    traces:\n      - R2.1\n      - R2.2\n  - id: AC3\n    criterion: \"Differential test against gbase64 passes for all required test cases.\"\n    traces:\n      - R1.1\n      - R1.2\n      - R1.3\n      - R1.4\n      - R2.1\n      - R2.2\n      - R2.3\n      - R2.4\n  - id: AC4\n    criterion: \"cmd/base64 compiles with no warnings under golangci-lint.\"\n    traces:\n      - R1.1\n      - R1.2\n      - R1.3\n      - R1.4\n      - R2.1\n      - R2.2\n      - R2.3\n      - R2.4\n      - R3.1\n      - R3.2\n      - R3.3\n","numLines":97,"startLine":1,"totalLines":97}}}
