ncoderConfig) error`\n     - `Decode(r io.Reader, w io.Writer, cfg DecoderConfig) error`\n\n4. Errors and fixes:\n   - No errors encountered yet — only file reads were performed before the summary was requested.\n\n5. Problem Solving:\n   The main problem to solve is modifying `cmd/base64/main.go` to support multiple file arguments processed sequentially as concatenated input. The current implementation:\n   - `parseArgs` returns a single file string\n   - `main` opens one file via `encutil.OpenInput`\n   \n   The solution needs to:\n   - Change `parseArgs` to return `[]string` (slice of files)\n   - In `main`, open all files and concatenate them using `io.MultiReader`\n   - Handle errors for each file individually (GNU format: \"base64: FILENAME: error\")\n   - If no files specified, default to stdin (empty string or \"-\")\n\n6. All user messages:\n   - Message 1: The complete stitch task description with all project context, SRDs, architecture, constitutions, requirements, acceptance criteria, and constraints for task #5520.\n   - Message 2: \"CRITICAL: Respond with TEXT ONLY. Do NOT call any tools.\" — requesting a detailed summary of the conversation.\n\n7. Pending Tasks:\n   - Modify `cmd/base64/main.go` to:\n     1. Change `parseArgs` to return `[]string` instead of single `string` for files\n     2. Update `main` to open multiple files and concatenate them via `io.MultiReader`\n     3. Ensure exit 0 on success, exit 1 on any failure\n     4. Ensure all error messages use GNU format \"base64: DESCRIPTION\"\n     5. Handle per-file open errors with \"base64: FILENAME: error\" format\n   - Run `go build -o bin/base64 ./cmd/base64/` to verify compilation\n   - Run `go vet ./cmd/base64/` to check for issues\n   - Run `go test ./cmd/base64/... -count=1` to verify tests pass\n\n8. Current Work:\n   I had just finished reading both required files (`srd080-base64.yaml` and `cmd/base64/main.go`) and was about to plan and implement the code changes to `cmd/base64/main.